Program Overview
What programs are being offered?
•	A Bachelor of Computer Science, which is a 3-year standalone degree focused on computer science fundamentals and emerging technologies.
•	A double degree combining a Bachelor of Computer Science with a Master of Data Science, completed over 4 years. The first three years focus on computer science, with the fourth year concentrating on data science.
•	The programs focus on emerging technologies and responsible innovation, including areas such as artificial intelligence, digital twins and other developing technologies.
How does this program compare to others?
•	The entry requirements are designed to make the program accessible to a broad range of students.
•	The curriculum emphasises responsible innovation and a range of emerging technologies rather than focusing solely on AI.
•	Industry engagement is integrated throughout the curriculum, providing students with exposure to real-world applications.
What are the key focus areas?
•	The program covers emerging technologies including artificial intelligence, data science and other developing areas of technology.
•	There is a strong emphasis on responsible innovation, including topics such as cybersecurity, digital trust and the ethical implications of technology.
•	The curriculum adopts a human-centred approach, focusing on how technology can be applied to real-world challenges.
Industry Partnerships
Which industry partners are involved?
•	Technology companies and industry organisations contribute to the program.
•	Industry partners provide input into curriculum design and help ensure course content remains relevant to current industry needs.
•	Opportunities may also exist for industry engagement through events, projects and other student activities.
What certifications can students earn?
•	Some course content is aligned with industry-standard technologies and professional certification requirements.
•	Completing relevant subjects can help prepare students to pursue external industry certifications.
What career opportunities are available?
•	The program aims to provide students with opportunities to gain practical industry experience.
•	Students develop skills relevant to a range of technology, data and digital roles.
•	Industry exposure throughout the degree can help students better understand workplace practices and expectations.
Curriculum and Teaching Approach
How is responsible innovation incorporated?
•	Ethical considerations are embedded throughout the curriculum.
•	Students learn frameworks for thinking about how technology should be developed and used responsibly.
•	Key concepts include accountability, privacy, accessibility and responsible use of AI and other technologies.
What is the teaching approach?
•	The program uses an active learning approach, incorporating a mix of independent learning, structured activities and applied tasks.
•	The curriculum is informed by current research and industry practices.
•	There is multidisciplinary collaboration across different areas of the university, giving students broader perspectives on technology and its applications.
What support is provided to students?
•	Students have access to a range of academic and student support services.
•	Support is designed to help students manage both academic requirements and their broader study experience.
•	Online students can access support through digital resources, webinars and individual assistance.
Program Differentiators
What makes this program unique?
•	Industry engagement is incorporated throughout the curriculum rather than being limited to occasional guest speakers.
•	The program covers a broad range of emerging technologies and prepares students for continued change within the technology sector.
•	There is a strong focus on responsible, ethical and human-centred approaches to technology.
•	The curriculum balances technical capabilities with broader professional and communication skills.
What research informs the curriculum?
•	The curriculum is informed by current research in areas such as cybersecurity, emerging technology and digital innovation.
•	Research helps ensure students are exposed to practical and contemporary applications of technology.
Target Audience
Who is the program aimed at?
•	The program is designed for both recent school leavers and people looking to develop or change their careers.
•	It aims to encourage participation from a diverse range of students and backgrounds.
•	Flexible study options support students who may not be able to attend traditional face-to-face classes.
•	The program may also appeal to organisations seeking to build technology and data capabilities within their workforce.
What motivates students to choose this program?
•	The combined degree provides a pathway to complete both undergraduate and postgraduate study within a streamlined timeframe.
•	Accessible entry requirements broaden the range of students who may be able to enter the program.
•	Students receive ongoing support throughout their studies.
•	The program is designed to build skills relevant to growing areas of the technology industry.
•	There is no advanced mathematics prerequisite, helping make the program accessible to students from a wider range of educational backgrounds.

